 "id": "bundle_s2_ndvi_monthly_ait_bouguemez",
 "title": "Catchment NDVI, Sentinel-2 monthly",
 "description": "Monthly NDVI over the Ait Bouguemez valley catchment (geo_ait_bouguemez_catchment revision 1) from Sentinel-2 L2A (Earth Search legacy sentinel-2-l2a), 2019-01 to 2025-12, at 10 m in EPSG:32629: per-pixel median of clear dates, area median and spatial IQR over pixels with at least 3 clear dates. A period is available when such pixels cover at least 70% of the catchment.\n\nReduced QA (scene classification only): snow and terrain shadow can survive the mask. The spatial IQR is variability across pixels, not a confidence interval. Item geometries are the catchment simplified to one DEM pixel; the exact frozen geometry is the analysis_geometry asset. The input set is exactly the derived_from items of each period: one item per tile and sensing date, the newest processing baseline, skipping a duplicate with no clear pixels over the catchment when a twin has some. Display rasters and value grids are not part of this version.\n\nRevision 13 (2026-10-27). Among duplicates of a tile and date, an item with no clear pixels over the catchment is now skipped when a twin has some. That clause was added to the duplicate rule after data was first read; the rule fixed before any data was read kept the newest processing baseline only. Revision 12, the first committed, has no version field; it documented the clause but kept the newest item, so it kept an item with 0 clear pixels over the catchment on seven tile-dates: 29RQQ 2019-04-17 (twin had 285 clear pixels), 2019-06-21 (702,669), 2020-11-12 (84), 2021-06-07 (8), 2021-11-19 (8), 2021-12-22 (8), and 29SQR 2020-10-23 (16). In five cases the twin is an older baseline (02.14, 03.00, 03.01), so its clear pixels come from an older scene classification. This revision recomputes 2019-04, 2019-06, 2020-10, 2020-11, 2021-06, 2021-11 and 2021-12 and everything derived from them; no NDVI or departure area median moved at four decimals.",
 "license": "other",
